# L §5.16 A random number of items: n = binomial(3, 1) draws 3 on every path, within the three slots: the total is
# cost[1] + cost[2] + cost[3] = 6 on every path, so its mean is 6, standard error 0 (q).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source src "s"
index slots = int 1..3
input trials: int
input cost[k in slots]: num
input n: dist
def total: num = sum(cost[k] for k in 1 .. n step 1)

ask q: mean(total) paths 20 seed 1

version v
  cite src
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  trials = 3
  cost[*] = 2
  n = binomial(trials, 1)
=== expect
q: 6 (standard error 0; 20 paths; horizon none)
  cut 2026-12-31
